From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: sunxi: cpu_comm: reserve TX FIFO room before publishing

The ARM -> MIPS msgbox FIFO holds eight words; the firmware's own send
waits while it is full. Our doorbell wrote without looking, so a word
written into a full FIFO would be lost after its message was already
published in shared memory. A count check alone cannot fix that: the
SENT flag is set before the doorbell, so refusing afterwards leaves a
publication the peer may act on.

Serialize the doorbell under one lock. This driver is the only writer
of the FIFO and the MIPS can only lower its count, so a count below the
depth observed under the lock reserves the word. Write the shared header
and its SENT flag inside that reservation, then the data word and the
TX_IRQ_EN pulse. When no room appears within 100 ms, return -EBUSY with
shared memory untouched; count refusals in tx_fifo_full. The lock also
stops two senders' data writes and pulses from interleaving. The pulse
itself is unchanged: whether the receiver needs the edge is unsettled.

Propagate the result. SendComm2CPUEx used to ignore SendCommLow's return,
turning any refusal into a 500-jiffy ACK timeout and a permanent
quarantine. A refused send now clears the pending ACK, removes and frees
the unpublished wait object, keeps the unpublished call slot cached for
the next send and releases the sequence semaphore. A failed copy_to_user
unwinds the same way instead of leaking its wait object; a partial
copy_from_user restores the cached slot's index. Only a published
message hands its slot to the peer.

SendAckLow now returns an error. A still-published previous ACK is
refused instead of BUG() in the receive thread; it, or a refused ACK
doorbell, quarantines sends to that peer like a missing CALL_ACK. A late
RETURN is recycled only after its RETURN_ACK was published.

Under the protocol's one-message-per-sequence gating at most four ARM
doorbell words are in flight, so a full FIFO needs leftover words, for
example from repeated module loads while the MIPS is parked. The guard
is defence in depth; the error paths are the substantive fix.

The FIFO depth check follows well0nez's 0014f; reserving before
publication, serialization and the error unwinding are ours.

Link: https://github.com/well0nez/allwinner-h713-linux/blob/149f51d0df24c45b12674c81aab128b1fc8f5d4b/mainline/patches/kernel/0014f-soc-sunxi-cpu-comm-never-write-into-a-full-tx-fifo.patch

